{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:c6929011b635a9cb","name":"Assault Droid Mark IV","source":{"id":"source:reference-c6929011b635a9cb","title":"Assault Droid Mark IV","revision":22069,"timestamp":"2024-08-30T19:29:07Z","sha256":"a9861b9d0a1dce9811dd3f8051d54090f0ebd461dc3f0de443471a9b11b666ba","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22069","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Assault%20Droid%20Mark%20IV&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-c6929011b635a9cb","blocks":["\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["Assault Droid Mark IV Units\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Assault Droid Mark IV Squad"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Assault_Droid_Mark_IV_Squad","referenceId":"reference:ac51cf0cd86a76be"},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["\n"]},"\n"],"colspan":2}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Assault Droid Mark IV Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Assault_Droid_Mark_IV_Battalion","referenceId":"reference:22947464f921465d"},"\n"],"colspan":2}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Originally created by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," in the days leading up to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", the Mark I and Mark IV Assault Droids are two of the most common Droid weapons in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"},". Though ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic","referenceId":"reference:6517b7e15507b001"}," still uses these Droids as automated defenses (patrolling city streets or military facilities), ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"}," puts the Droids to greater use. In the early days of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Civil War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Civil_War"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith_Empire","referenceId":"reference:303e4cc32aa1a8e1"}," rely heavily on Assault Droids to fill out the ranks of their military, as it takes time for members of the Republic to defect and join the Empire. As the Sith Academy on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Korriban"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Korriban","referenceId":"reference:e5de27f696051005"}," cranks out more recruits, Assault Droids fall back into an auxiliary role, but are still used as the defenders of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," throughout the Sith fleet.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Though Czerka manufactures several models of Assault Droids, the Mark I and Mark IV models are the most sought after. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Assault Droid Mark I"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Assault_Droid_Mark_I","referenceId":"reference:b70dbe8cd5fae60e"}," is a unique design that, while vaguely humanoid, relies on a single leg for the bulk of its motion. The Assault Droid Mark IV is more spiderlike, with four legs and a head with a mounted ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Rifle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Rifle","referenceId":"reference:fb78a988cbf9557f"},". Both the Mark I and Mark IV Droids are capable defenders, but they have little in the way of advanced tactical programming. These Droids are used primarily in a reactive, defensive manner and, despite their simple programming, have proven exceptionally capable of repelling Republic boarding parties attempting to seize Sith ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mark IV Assault Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Assault Droid Mark IV Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +12; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +12\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic (understand only), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_De